; A walk through a forest at dusk. A river winds through the trees, with gravel and pebbles on its banks and in its bed, and grass
; everywhere else. A dirt path leads to a wooden bridge over the river, and a standing torch lights the bridge. Glowing insects fly
; around the river, each with a light that moves with it. The scene has hundreds of trees (separate entities), grass tufts and pebbles
; (merged into a few dozen meshes by area, so that parts out of view are skipped), one see-through water ribbon, and glowing sprites.
; Everything is made in code: the meshes, the textures and the positions, there are no files.
; Needs a window and a GPU: python3 benchmarks/forest.py builds and runs it, under xvfb and llvmpipe if there is no display.
;
; Environment variables:
;   BENCH_TREES    how many trees are made (default 1800)
;   BENCH_GRASS    how many blades of grass are made (default 600000, in clumps, in the area the camera walks through; each is opaque, 5 vertices, 0.25 to 1.9 units tall; only the tip of a blade moves in the wind, in the areas within 45 units of the camera)
;   BENCH_LEAVES   single leaves on each twig (default 18)
;   BENCH_PEBBLES  how many pebbles are made (default 14000: gravel and stones, 6 vertices each)
;   BENCH_INSECTS  how many glowing insects fly around (default 40; each has a glow sprite)
;   BENCH_INSECT_LIGHTS  how many of them have a light too (default 6): a graphics card has 8 lights, and the scene has a moon and a torch as well. The
;                  original Blitz3D lights with the first 8 lights in the order they were made, BlitzLLVM with the 8 nearest.
;   BENCH_FRAMES   how many frames are timed (default 600)
;   BENCH_WARMUP   frames that are rendered but not timed, they make the GPU buffers (default 5)
;   BENCH_START    frame number the walk and the insects start at (default 0, other values are for screenshots)
;   BENCH_VIEWRIVER  1 puts the camera on the bridge, looking down the river, 2 at the torch, for screenshots (default 0)
;   BENCH_BLOOM    1 draws the fullscreen bloom (default), 0 leaves it out
;   BENCH_BLOOM_GAIN  how many times the blur is added to the picture (default 1)
;   BENCH_SEED     seed of the random placement (default 1)
;   BENCH_W, BENCH_H  size of the window (default 640 x 360)
;   BENCH_SHOT     file to save the last frame to (optional)
;   BENCH_RESULT   file to write the RESULT line to (optional, it is also in the debug log)
;   BENCH_FRAMETIMES  file to write the time of every frame to, in microseconds, one per line (optional)
;
; The camera walks to the bridge and back along the path, 1200 frames for the round trip. Where everything is depends only on the seed and the
; frame number, so the picture is the same on every run and every machine.

; Runs with BlitzLLVM and with the original Blitz3D, so that their speeds can be compared. What the original does not have (a
; microsecond timer, the draw counters) is in forest_llvm.bi or forest_original.bi, python3 benchmarks/forest.py copies the right
; one next to this file as forest_counters.bi.
Include "forest_counters.bi"

; The world is 160 x 160 units, from -80 to 80. The water is at height 0, the river bed at -1.5, the banks and the ground near the path at 1.
Const WORLD# = 80.0
Const WATERY# = 0.0
Const BEDY# = -1.5
Const BANKY# = 1.0
Const DECKY# = 1.2
Const BRIDGEHALF# = 6.4

Global BridgeX# = 0
Global leaftexture = 0
; A leaf card is this much of the size a twig is given: one leaf is about 0.45 units long (the card holds a leaf of 0.85 of its width).
Const LEAFSCALE# = 0.3
Global TrunkPh# = 0
Global TrunkAmp# = 0
Global MoonX# = 0
Global MoonY# = 0
Global MoonZ# = 0
Global TorchX# = 0
Global TorchY# = 0
Global TorchZ# = 0
Global water = 0
Global watersurf = 0
Global NormalGround = 0
Global AlbedoBark = 0
Global AlbedoBirch = 0
Global AlbedoChar = 0
Global AlbedoTorch = 0
Global NormalBark = 0
Global NormalPlanks = 0
Global AlbedoPlanks = 0
Global CR# = 0
Global CG# = 0
Global CB# = 0

Function Env$(name$, fallback$)
	value$ = GetEnv$(name$)
	If value$ = "" Then value$ = fallback$
	Return value$
End Function

; The random numbers come from this generator and not from Rnd, because Rnd gives different numbers in BlitzLLVM and in the
; original Blitz3D, and then the two would not draw the same scene. It is the Park-Miller generator, with Schrage's way of
; multiplying without leaving 31 bits, so it gives the same numbers in both. Never two calls as arguments of one call: the
; original evaluates arguments in another order.
Global BenchState = 1

Function BenchSeedRnd(seed)
	BenchState = (seed Mod 2147483646) + 1
	If BenchState < 1 Then BenchState = BenchState + 2147483646
End Function

Function BenchRnd#(low#, high#)
	BenchState = 16807 * (BenchState Mod 127773) - 2836 * (BenchState / 127773)
	If BenchState <= 0 Then BenchState = BenchState + 2147483647
	Return low + (high - low) * (BenchState / 2147483647.0)
End Function

Function FMax#(a#, b#)
	If a > b Then Return a
	Return b
End Function

Function FMin#(a#, b#)
	If a < b Then Return a
	Return b
End Function

Function Lerp#(a#, b#, t#)
	Return a + (b - a) * t
End Function

Function Smooth#(t#)
	If t < 0 Then t = 0
	If t > 1 Then t = 1
	Return t * t * (3 - 2 * t)
End Function

; A smooth pattern between -1 and 1 that does not need a table, for the color of the ground.
Function Noise#(x#, z#)
	Return Sin(x * 41 + z * 17) * 0.5 + Sin(x * 13 - z * 37) * 0.3 + Sin(x * 5 + z * 7) * 0.2
End Function

; The center line of the river, which flows along z. At z = 0 it is at the top of a bend, so that the bridge crosses where it runs straight.
Function RiverX#(z#)
	Return 9 * Cos(z * 2.4) + 2.5 * Cos(z * 6.7) - 5
End Function

; The center line of the path, which runs along x with some turns, and comes straight to the bridge at z = 0.
Function PathZ#(x#)
	d# = x - BridgeX
	Return 6 * Sin(d * 3.2) * Smooth(Abs(d) / 14)
End Function

; Height of the ground: the river bed with banks that rise to 1 at 6 units from the middle, and low hills further away, except at the path.
Function Height#(x#, z#)
	d# = Abs(x - RiverX(z))
	dp# = Abs(z - PathZ(x))
	hills# = Smooth((d - 5) / 12) * Smooth((dp - 1) / 5)
	base# = BANKY + hills * (1.6 * Sin(x * 3.1) * Cos(z * 2.6) + 0.8 * Sin(x * 7 + z * 5))
	t# = Smooth((d - 2.4) / 3.6)
	bed# = BEDY + 0.2 * Sin(x * 20 + z * 13)
	Return bed + (base - bed) * t
End Function

; Where the camera's feet are: the ground, or the boards on the bridge.
Function GroundY#(x#, z#)
	h# = Height(x, z)
	w# = Smooth((BRIDGEHALF + 1.5 - Abs(x - BridgeX)) / 1.5) * Smooth(2.0 - Abs(z))
	Return FMax(h, Lerp(h, DECKY, w))
End Function

; The color of the ground at a place: grass, gravel and sand on the banks, mud under the water, and the dirt of the path on top.
Function GroundColor(x#, z#, h#)
	n# = Noise(x, z)
	d# = Abs(x - RiverX(z))
	dp# = Abs(z - PathZ(x))
	r# = 48 + 14 * n
	g# = 98 + 20 * n
	b# = 36 + 8 * n
	; Gravel at the water, dark grey with a few reddish and bluish patches, and it thins out into the grass.
	wet# = 1 - Smooth((d - 4.6) / 3)
	tintn# = Sin(x * 5.3 + z * 3.1) * Sin(x * 2.1 - z * 4.7)
	r = Lerp(r, 70 + 16 * n + 14 * tintn, wet)
	g = Lerp(g, 68 + 16 * n, wet)
	b = Lerp(b, 66 + 16 * n - 14 * tintn, wet)
	mud# = 1 - Smooth((h - 0.1) / 0.7)
	r = Lerp(r, 66 + 8 * n, mud)
	g = Lerp(g, 60 + 8 * n, mud)
	b = Lerp(b, 48 + 6 * n, mud)
	p# = 1 - Smooth((dp - 1.3) / 1.2)
	p = p * (1 - mud)
	r = Lerp(r, 118 + 18 * n, p)
	g = Lerp(g, 88 + 14 * n, p)
	b = Lerp(b, 58 + 10 * n, p)
	CR = r : CG = g : CB = b
End Function

; The ground: a grid of 0.8 x 0.8 units. The color of every vertex is not a color but the direction of the light in the frame of the bump map (see BumpColor);
; what the ground looks like is in the textures: a bump map that repeats every 4 units, and a picture of the whole world (made in MakeGroundPicture).
Function MakeTerrain()
	m = CreateMesh()
	n = 200
	cell# = WORLD * 2 / n
	; Four bands, one surface each: one surface of 80000 triangles is more than the 65535 primitives a Direct3D 7 draw call can have, and the original Blitz3D then
	; draws nothing of it.
	For band = 0 To 3
		s = CreateSurface(m)
		z0 = band * 50
		For iz = z0 To z0 + 50
			For ix = 0 To n
				x# = -WORLD + ix * cell
				z# = -WORLD + iz * cell
				h# = Height(x, z)
				; The slope gives the frame the bump map is in: tangent along +x, bitangent along +z, normal up.
				hx# = (Height(x + 0.4, z) - Height(x - 0.4, z)) / 0.8
				hz# = (Height(x, z + 0.4) - Height(x, z - 0.4)) / 0.8
				il# = 1 / Sqr(1 + hx * hx)
				jl# = 1 / Sqr(1 + hz * hz)
				nl# = 1 / Sqr(1 + hx * hx + hz * hz)
				v = AddVertex(s, x, h, z, x / 4, z / 4)
				VertexTexCoords s, v, (x + WORLD) / (2 * WORLD), (z + WORLD) / (2 * WORLD), 0, 1
				BumpColor x, h, z, il, hx * il, 0, 0, hz * jl, jl, -hx * nl, nl, -hz * nl, 1
				VertexColor s, v, CR, CG, CB
			Next
		Next
		For iz = 0 To 49
			For ix = 0 To n - 1
				a = iz * (n + 1) + ix
				b = a + 1
				c = a + n + 1
				d = c + 1
				AddTriangle s, a, c, b
				AddTriangle s, b, c, d
			Next
		Next
	Next
	Return m
End Function

; The water: a ribbon along the river, 10 units wide (6 vertices across, 161 along), at the height of the water. The banks hide the sides of it. Every frame the vertices
; move in waves that run down the river (RunWater), and the picture of the water is made new every frame on the GPU, so the river flows (v is 1 unit for 10 units of river, the same as the 10 units across it).
Function MakeWater()
	m = CreateMesh()
	s = CreateSurface(m)
	For i = 0 To 160
		z# = -WORLD + i
		x# = RiverX(z)
		For c = 0 To 5
			AddVertex s, x - 5 + c * 2, WATERY, z, c / 5.0, z / 10
		Next
	Next
	For i = 0 To 159
		For c = 0 To 4
			a = i * 6 + c
			AddTriangle s, a, a + 6, a + 1
			AddTriangle s, a + 1, a + 6, a + 7
		Next
	Next
	UpdateNormals m
	Return m
End Function

; The night sky, painted on a sphere around the camera: a dark blue that gets lighter at the horizon, a faint band of the milky way and about 1600 stars of one texel each (a
; few of them brighter). The generator places them.
Function MakeStars()
	t = CreateTexture(2048, 1024, 1)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 1023
		e# = Abs(y - 511.5) / 511.5
		For x = 0 To 2047
			band# = Sin(x * 360.0 / 2048 + y * 0.175)
			band = 1 - Abs(band + 0.2 * Sin(x * 1.55)) * 3
			If band < 0 Then band = 0
			bl# = band * (1 - e) * 14 * (0.6 + 0.4 * Sin(x * 5.5 + y * 3.5))
			r = Int(10 - 8 * e + bl * 0.5)
			g = Int(15 - 12 * e + bl * 0.6)
			b = Int(30 - 22 * e + bl * 0.8)
			WritePixelFast x, y, $FF000000 Or (r Shl 16) Or (g Shl 8) Or b, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	For k = 0 To 1599
		sx = 1 + Int(BenchRnd(0, 2045))
		sy = 8 + Int(BenchRnd(0, 1007))
		c = 140 + ((k * 37) Mod 116)
		tint = (k Mod 5)
		If k Mod 9 = 0 Then c = 255 Else c = c * 0.8
		r = c : g = c : b = c
		If tint = 0 Then r = c * 0.8 : g = c * 0.9
		If tint = 1 Then g = c * 0.9 : b = c * 0.75
		WritePixelFast sx, sy, $FF000000 Or (Int(r) Shl 16) Or (Int(g) Shl 8) Or Int(b), TextureBuffer(t)
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; The full moon, as seen with the eye: a pale disc whose big dark seas have uneven edges, dozens of craters of all sizes (a darker floor, a bright rim), fine grain, and a little darkening
; at the edge. Nothing around it: no glow. The craters and seas are placed by the generator of the scene (in the same order every time).
; The moon's brightness per texel (the original needs arrays to be declared in the main program).
Dim lum#(255, 255)

Function MakeMoon()
	t = CreateTexture(256, 256, 3)
	For y = 0 To 255
		For x = 0 To 255
			px# = (x - 127.5) / 121.0
			py# = (y - 127.5) / 121.0
			grain# = 1 + 0.035 * Sin(x * 97 + y * 53) * Sin(x * 41 - y * 89)
			; Seas: big ellipses with wobbling edges and soft sides.
			dark# = 0
			For k = 0 To 5
				Select k
					Case 0
						ecx# = -0.28 : ecy# = -0.3 : erx# = 0.36 : ery# = 0.26
					Case 1
						ecx = 0.16 : ecy = -0.22 : erx = 0.26 : ery = 0.3
					Case 2
						ecx = -0.12 : ecy = 0.12 : erx = 0.3 : ery = 0.2
					Case 3
						ecx = 0.32 : ecy = 0.14 : erx = 0.18 : ery = 0.17
					Case 4
						ecx = -0.45 : ecy = 0.18 : erx = 0.14 : ery = 0.2
					Default
						ecx = 0.04 : ecy = 0.55 : erx = 0.22 : ery = 0.1
				End Select
				qx# = (px - ecx) / erx
				qy# = (py - ecy) / ery
				q# = Sqr(qx * qx + qy * qy) + 0.12 * Sin(px * 40 + k * 70) * Sin(py * 33 + k * 30) + 0.07 * Sin(px * 91 - py * 77 + k * 20)
				m# = 1 - Smooth((q - 0.65) / 0.5)
				If m > dark Then dark = m
			Next
			lum(x, y) = (226 - 80 * dark) * grain
		Next
	Next
	; Craters: many small ones, a few big ones, each with a dark floor and a bright rim.
	For k = 1 To 170
		ang# = BenchRnd(0, 360)
		dist# = Sqr(BenchRnd(0, 0.72))
		cx# = Cos(ang) * dist
		cy# = Sin(ang) * dist
		r# = BenchRnd(0, 1)
		cr# = 0.012 + r * r * r * 0.085
		x0 = Int((cx - cr * 1.4) * 121 + 127.5)
		x1 = Int((cx + cr * 1.4) * 121 + 127.5)
		y0 = Int((cy - cr * 1.4) * 121 + 127.5)
		y1 = Int((cy + cr * 1.4) * 121 + 127.5)
		For y = y0 To y1
			For x = x0 To x1
				If x >= 0 And x < 256 And y >= 0 And y < 256 Then
					dx# = ((x - 127.5) / 121.0 - cx) / cr
					dy# = ((y - 127.5) / 121.0 - cy) / cr
					d# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy)
					If d < 0.85 Then
						lum(x, y) = lum(x, y) * 0.9
					ElseIf d < 1.25 Then
						lum(x, y) = lum(x, y) + 20 * (1 - Abs(d - 1.05) / 0.2) * (0.6 + 0.4 * dx)
					EndIf
				EndIf
			Next
		Next
	Next
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 255
		For x = 0 To 255
			px# = (x - 127.5) / 121.0
			py# = (y - 127.5) / 121.0
			r# = Sqr(px * px + py * py)
			a# = 1 - (r - 0.97) / 0.03
			If a > 1 Then a = 1
			If a < 0 Then a = 0
			c# = lum(x, y) * (1 - 0.3 * r * r * r)
			If c > 255 Then c = 255
			If c < 0 Then c = 0
			WritePixelFast x, y, (Int(a * 255) Shl 24) Or (Int(c * 0.97) Shl 16) Or (Int(c * 0.98) Shl 8) Or Int(c * 0.93), TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; A bump map, which is a picture of normals in the frame of the surface: red is the part that points along the texture's u direction, green along v, blue away from
; the surface, and flat is (128, 128, 255). Kind 0 is bumpy ground, 1 bark (ridges along v) and 2 boards (grain along u, a groove at both edges in v).
; All of them repeat every 128 pixels so that they can be laid side by side.
Function BumpHeight#(kind, x, y)
	u# = (x Mod 128) * 360.0 / 128
	v# = (y Mod 128) * 360.0 / 128
	Select kind
		Case 0
			Return Sin(u * 4 + Sin(v * 3) * 40) * 0.5 + Sin(v * 6 + Sin(u * 2) * 30) * 0.4 + Sin(u * 11 + v * 9) * 0.12
		Case 1
			Return Sin(u * 5 + Sin(v * 2) * 50) * 0.7 + Sin(u * 11 + Sin(v * 3) * 30) * 0.3 + 0.3 * Sin(v * 7 + u * 2)
		Default
			h# = Sin(v * 8 + Sin(u * 2) * 20) * 0.4 + Sin(v * 21 + u) * 0.15
			e# = (y Mod 128)
			If e < 5 Or e > 122 Then h = h - 1.6
			Return h
	End Select
End Function

Function MakeNormalMap(kind)
	t = CreateTexture(128, 128, 1 + 8)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	strength# = 0.2
	If kind = 1 Then strength = 1.5
	If kind = 2 Then strength = 0.9
	For y = 0 To 127
		For x = 0 To 127
			dx# = (BumpHeight(kind, x + 1, y) - BumpHeight(kind, x + 127, y)) * strength
			dy# = (BumpHeight(kind, x, y + 1) - BumpHeight(kind, x, y + 127)) * strength
			l# = 1 / Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1)
			r = Int(127.5 - 127.5 * dx * l)
			g = Int(127.5 - 127.5 * dy * l)
			b = Int(127.5 + 127.5 * l)
			WritePixelFast x, y, $FF000000 Or (r Shl 16) Or (g Shl 8) Or b, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	TextureBlend t, 4
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; What the bumps are painted: kind 0 brown bark, 1 birch (pale, with dark marks across), 3 charred, wrapped wood with a few glowing cracks, 4 warm bark for the torch, anything else weathered boards with moss. The color comes from the same heights as the bumps, so that the
; grooves are dark.
Function MakeAlbedo(kind)
	t = CreateTexture(128, 128, 1 + 8)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 127
		For x = 0 To 127
			Select kind
				Case 0
					h# = BumpHeight(1, x, y)
					k# = 0.62 + 0.3 * h
					r = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 112 * k * 1.5))) : g = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 82 * k * 1.5))) : b = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 54 * k * 1.5)))
				Case 1
					h = BumpHeight(1, x, y)
					k = 0.92 + 0.08 * h
					mark# = Sin(y * 360.0 / 128 * 5 + x * 7) * Sin(x * 360.0 / 128 * 2 + 40)
					If mark > 0.72 Then k = k * 0.35
					r = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 215 * k))) : g = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 210 * k))) : b = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 196 * k)))
				Case 4
					h = BumpHeight(1, x, y)
					k = 0.62 + 0.3 * h
					r = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 112 * k * 2.6))) : g = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 82 * k * 2.0))) : b = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 54 * k * 1.3)))
				Case 3
					h = BumpHeight(1, x, y)
					k = 0.9 + 0.25 * h
					r = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 80 * k))) : g = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 52 * k))) : b = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 38 * k)))
					If h > 0.85 Then r = Int(FMin(255, r + 90)) : g = Int(FMin(255, g + 30))
				Default
					h = BumpHeight(2, x, y)
					k = 0.78 + 0.2 * h
					r = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 112 * k))) : g = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 98 * k))) : b = Int(FMax(0, FMin(255, 82 * k)))
					moss# = Sin(x * 360.0 / 128 * 3 + y * 5) * Sin(y * 360.0 / 128 * 2 + x * 3) + 0.5 * Sin(x * 360.0 / 128 * 7 - y * 9)
					If moss > 0.45 Then
						ms# = FMin(1, (moss - 0.45) * 3)
						r = Int(Lerp(r, 58 * k, ms)) : g = Int(Lerp(g, 82 * k, ms)) : b = Int(Lerp(b, 36 * k, ms))
					EndIf
			End Select
			WritePixelFast x, y, $FF000000 Or (r Shl 16) Or (g Shl 8) Or b, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; A picture of the ground of the whole world from above, 512 x 512 texels. The colors of GroundColor, with fine grain on them, and the light that does not change
; painted in: the cold light of the moon everywhere, and the warm light of the torch around it. (With bump mapping the vertices carry the direction of the light,
; so the color of the light has to be in a texture.) Set 1 of the coordinates of the terrain is where it goes.
Function MakeGroundPicture()
	t = CreateTexture(512, 512, 1 + 8)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	texel# = WORLD * 2 / 512
	For py = 0 To 511
		z# = -WORLD + (py + 0.5) * texel
		For px = 0 To 511
			x# = -WORLD + (px + 0.5) * texel
			h# = Height(x, z)
			GroundColor x, z, h
			grain# = 1 + 0.1 * Sin(x * 97 + z * 61) * Sin(x * 53 - z * 89)
			dx# = x - TorchX
			dy# = h - TorchY
			dz# = z - TorchZ
			dist# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
			w# = 1 - dist / 16
			If w < 0 Then w = 0
			w = w * w * 1.4
			r = Int(FMin(255, CR * grain * (0.95 + w * 1.6)))
			g = Int(FMin(255, CG * grain * (1.28 + w * 0.9)))
			b = Int(FMin(255, CB * grain * (1.45 + w * 0.4)))
			WritePixelFast px, py, $FF000000 Or (r Shl 16) Or (g Shl 8) Or b, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	TextureCoords t, 1
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; One face of a box, the corners clockwise as seen from outside.
Function AddQuad(s, ax#, ay#, az#, bx#, by#, bz#, cx#, cy#, cz#, dx#, dy#, dz#, r, g, b)
	v = AddVertex(s, ax, ay, az)
	VertexColor s, v, r, g, b
	v1 = AddVertex(s, bx, by, bz)
	VertexColor s, v1, r, g, b
	v2 = AddVertex(s, cx, cy, cz)
	VertexColor s, v2, r, g, b
	v3 = AddVertex(s, dx, dy, dz)
	VertexColor s, v3, r, g, b
	AddTriangle s, v, v1, v2
	AddTriangle s, v, v2, v3
End Function

; A box with all six faces (the sides get a little darker than the top so that it looks like a box in any light).
Function AddBox(s, x0#, y0#, z0#, x1#, y1#, z1#, r, g, b)
	AddQuad s, x0, y1, z0, x0, y1, z1, x1, y1, z1, x1, y1, z0, r, g, b
	AddQuad s, x0, y0, z0, x1, y0, z0, x1, y0, z1, x0, y0, z1, r * 0.6, g * 0.6, b * 0.6
	AddQuad s, x1, y0, z1, x1, y1, z1, x0, y1, z1, x0, y0, z1, r * 0.85, g * 0.85, b * 0.85
	AddQuad s, x0, y0, z0, x0, y1, z0, x1, y1, z0, x1, y0, z0, r * 0.85, g * 0.85, b * 0.85
	AddQuad s, x1, y0, z0, x1, y1, z0, x1, y1, z1, x1, y0, z1, r * 0.75, g * 0.75, b * 0.75
	AddQuad s, x0, y0, z1, x0, y1, z1, x0, y1, z0, x0, y0, z0, r * 0.75, g * 0.75, b * 0.75
End Function

; Bump mapping the way Direct3D 7 does it, which is how the original Blitz3D does it (TextureBlend 4): the color of a vertex is not a color but the direction of the light
; at the vertex in the frame of the surface (t along u of the bump map, b along v, n out of the surface), written as 127.5 + 127.5 * direction; the bump map
; is the first texture (blend 4, dot3) and the picture that is seen the second. The direction is the sum of the moon, a little light from everywhere
; (along the normal) and the torch (with the distance), and it is fixed: the flicker of the torch and the lights of the insects do not light bumped things, and the
; objects that have bumps must not turn (so the trees stand straight). The result goes in CR, CG and CB.
Function BumpColor(px#, py#, pz#, tx#, ty#, tz#, bx#, by#, bz#, nx#, ny#, nz#, torch)
	lx# = MoonX * 0.8 + nx * 0.8
	ly# = MoonY * 0.8 + ny * 0.8
	lz# = MoonZ * 0.8 + nz * 0.8
	If torch = 1 Then
		dx# = TorchX - px
		dy# = TorchY - py
		dz# = TorchZ - pz
		dist# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
		If dist < 16 And dist > 0.001 Then
			w# = 1 - dist / 16
			w = w * w * 1.3 / dist
			lx = lx + dx * w
			ly = ly + dy * w
			lz = lz + dz * w
		EndIf
	EndIf
	a# = lx * tx + ly * ty + lz * tz
	b# = lx * bx + ly * by + lz * bz
	c# = lx * nx + ly * ny + lz * nz + 0.3
	If a > 1 Then a = 1
	If a < -1 Then a = -1
	If b > 1 Then b = 1
	If b < -1 Then b = -1
	If c > 1 Then c = 1
	If c < -1 Then c = -1
	CR = 127.5 + 127.5 * a
	CG = 127.5 + 127.5 * b
	CB = 127.5 + 127.5 * c
End Function

; One face for bump mapping, the corners clockwise as seen from outside (a is bottom left, b top left, c top right, d bottom right, as in AddQuad) and n where it faces.
; The long side of the face is u (the grain of the boards runs along it), the short side v, and v goes from 0 to 1 across the short side.
Function AddQuadB(s, ax#, ay#, az#, bx#, by#, bz#, cx#, cy#, cz#, dx#, dy#, dz#, nx#, ny#, nz#)
	ux# = dx - ax : uy# = dy - ay : uz# = dz - az
	vx# = bx - ax : vy# = by - ay : vz# = bz - az
	lu# = Sqr(ux * ux + uy * uy + uz * uz)
	lv# = Sqr(vx * vx + vy * vy + vz * vz)
	If lv > lu Then
		; The other way round: u along the long side.
		tx# = ux : ty# = uy : tz# = uz
		ux = vx : uy = vy : uz = vz
		vx = tx : vy = ty : vz = tz
		t# = lu : lu = lv : lv = t
	EndIf
	tx = ux / lu : ty = uy / lu : tz = uz / lu
	bx2# = vx / lv : by2# = vy / lv : bz2# = vz / lv
	base = CountVertices(s)
	For k = 0 To 3
		Select k
			Case 0
				px# = ax : py# = ay : pz# = az
			Case 1
				px = bx : py = by : pz = bz
			Case 2
				px = cx : py = cy : pz = cz
			Default
				px = dx : py = dy : pz = dz
		End Select
		qx# = px - ax : qy# = py - ay : qz# = pz - az
		u# = (qx * tx + qy * ty + qz * tz) * 0.7
		v# = (qx * bx2 + qy * by2 + qz * bz2) / lv
		vert = AddVertex(s, px, py, pz, u, v)
		BumpColor px, py, pz, tx, ty, tz, bx2, by2, bz2, nx, ny, nz, 1
		VertexColor s, vert, CR, CG, CB
	Next
	AddTriangle s, base, base + 1, base + 2
	AddTriangle s, base, base + 2, base + 3
End Function

Function AddBoxB(s, x0#, y0#, z0#, x1#, y1#, z1#)
	AddQuadB s, x0, y1, z0, x0, y1, z1, x1, y1, z1, x1, y1, z0, 0, 1, 0
	AddQuadB s, x0, y0, z0, x1, y0, z0, x1, y0, z1, x0, y0, z1, 0, -1, 0
	AddQuadB s, x1, y0, z1, x1, y1, z1, x0, y1, z1, x0, y0, z1, 0, 0, 1
	AddQuadB s, x0, y0, z0, x0, y1, z0, x1, y1, z0, x1, y0, z0, 0, 0, -1
	AddQuadB s, x1, y0, z0, x1, y1, z0, x1, y1, z1, x1, y0, z1, 1, 0, 0
	AddQuadB s, x0, y0, z1, x0, y1, z1, x0, y1, z0, x0, y0, z0, -1, 0, 0
End Function

; A cone, open at the bottom, with rings of segs corners. The color goes from (r0, g0, b0) at the bottom to (r1, g1, b1) at the tip.
Function AddCone(s, cx#, y0#, cz#, rad#, h#, segs, r0, g0, b0, r1, g1, b1)
	base = CountVertices(s)
	For i = 0 To segs - 1
		a# = i * 360.0 / segs
		v = AddVertex(s, cx + Cos(a) * rad, y0, cz + Sin(a) * rad)
		VertexColor s, v, r0, g0, b0
	Next
	tip = AddVertex(s, cx, y0 + h, cz)
	VertexColor s, tip, r1, g1, b1
	For i = 0 To segs - 1
		AddTriangle s, base + i, tip, base + ((i + 1) Mod segs)
	Next
End Function

; A blob (two cones base to base) with its widest part at height y.
Function AddBlob(s, cx#, y#, cz#, rad#, h#, segs, r, g, b)
	base = CountVertices(s)
	For i = 0 To segs - 1
		a# = i * 360.0 / segs + 17
		v = AddVertex(s, cx + Cos(a) * rad, y, cz + Sin(a) * rad)
		VertexColor s, v, r, g, b
	Next
	top = AddVertex(s, cx, y + h, cz)
	VertexColor s, top, r * 1.25, g * 1.25, b * 1.1
	bottom = AddVertex(s, cx, y - h * 0.7, cz)
	VertexColor s, bottom, r * 0.55, g * 0.55, b * 0.55
	For i = 0 To segs - 1
		AddTriangle s, base + i, top, base + ((i + 1) Mod segs)
		AddTriangle s, base + i, base + ((i + 1) Mod segs), bottom
	Next
End Function

; The wind moves the leaves and the thin branches of the trees (a thick branch, or the trunk, stays where it is). The trees are copies of nine templates that share their mesh, so a template sways
; as a whole: while a template is made, every vertex that moves is written down here (the surface it is in, its number, where it is, and how much it moves, 0 to 1). Dim arrays have to be
; declared in the main program for the original Blitz3D, so they are here, before the functions that fill them.
Const SWAYMAX = 400000
Dim SwSurf(SWAYMAX)
Dim SwIdx(SWAYMAX)
Dim SwX#(SWAYMAX)
Dim SwY#(SWAYMAX)
Dim SwZ#(SWAYMAX)
Dim SwW#(SWAYMAX)
Dim TplFirst(8)
Dim TplCount(8)
Global SwayN = 0
Global CurTpl = 0
Global SwayOn = 1

; How much a place on a tree moves: nothing at the trunk, more further out and higher up.
Function Flex#(x#, y#, z#)
	f# = (Sqr(x * x + z * z) - 0.2) / 2.2 + (y - 2.0) * 0.03
	If f < 0 Then f = 0
	If f > 1 Then f = 1
	Return f
End Function

Function SwayAdd(sf, idx, x#, y#, z#, w#)
	If CurTpl > 0 And SwayOn = 1 And w > 0.02 And SwayN < SWAYMAX Then
		SwSurf(SwayN) = sf
		SwIdx(SwayN) = idx
		SwX(SwayN) = x
		SwY(SwayN) = y
		SwZ(SwayN) = z
		SwW(SwayN) = w
		SwayN = SwayN + 1
	EndIf
End Function

; One leaf: a card of 2 x sz with one of the four leaf shapes of the leaf texture (cell 0 to 3), one face (the leaf mesh is drawn with culling off). The stem of the leaf is at
; (ax, ay, az), the leaf grows from there in direction (ux, uy, uz) (its length is 2 x sz x 0.88) and its blade is wide in direction (vx, vy, vz), both unit vectors at right angles.
; It is lit as if it faced away from the middle of the crown (nx, ny, nz) so that the crown shades as a whole.
Function AddLeaf(s, ax#, ay#, az#, ux#, uy#, uz#, vx#, vy#, vz#, sz#, nx#, ny#, nz#, r, g, b, cell)
	u0# = (cell And 1) * 0.5
	v0# = (cell Shr 1) * 0.5
	cx# = ax + ux * sz * 0.88
	cy# = ay + uy * sz * 0.88
	cz# = az + uz * sz * 0.88
	base = CountVertices(s)
	v = AddVertex(s, cx - ux * sz - vx * sz, cy - uy * sz - vy * sz, cz - uz * sz - vz * sz, u0, v0 + 0.5)
	v = AddVertex(s, cx + ux * sz - vx * sz, cy + uy * sz - vy * sz, cz + uz * sz - vz * sz, u0 + 0.5, v0 + 0.5)
	v = AddVertex(s, cx + ux * sz + vx * sz, cy + uy * sz + vy * sz, cz + uz * sz + vz * sz, u0 + 0.5, v0)
	v = AddVertex(s, cx - ux * sz + vx * sz, cy - uy * sz + vy * sz, cz - uz * sz + vz * sz, u0, v0)
	For k = 0 To 3
		VertexNormal s, base + k, nx, ny, nz
		VertexColor s, base + k, r, g, b
		SwayAdd s, base + k, VertexX(s, base + k), VertexY(s, base + k), VertexZ(s, base + k), Flex(cx, cy, cz)
	Next
	AddTriangle s, base, base + 3, base + 1
	AddTriangle s, base + 1, base + 3, base + 2
End Function

; A branch: a tapering tube from one point to another with sides sides, with the bump frame of the surface on every vertex (u round it, twice; v along it, 0.5 per
; unit), so that the bark has the same bumps as the trunk.
Function AddBranch(s, x0#, y0#, z0#, x1#, y1#, z1#, r0#, r1#, sides)
	dx# = x1 - x0
	dy# = y1 - y0
	dz# = z1 - z0
	length# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
	dx = dx / length : dy = dy / length : dz = dz / length
	If Abs(dy) > 0.95 Then
		e1x# = 1 : e1y# = 0 : e1z# = 0
	Else
		n# = Sqr(dx * dx + dz * dz)
		e1x = -dz / n : e1y = 0 : e1z = dx / n
	EndIf
	e2x# = e1y * dz - e1z * dy
	e2y# = e1z * dx - e1x * dz
	e2z# = e1x * dy - e1y * dx
	; Texels have the same size everywhere: the texture goes round a whole number of times and is as long as it is wide.
	circ# = 6.2832 * (r0 + r1) * 0.5
	repeats = Int(circ / 0.5 + 0.5)
	If repeats < 1 Then repeats = 1
	tile# = circ / repeats
	base = CountVertices(s)
	For ring = 0 To 1
		For i = 0 To sides
			a# = i * 360.0 / sides
			ox# = Cos(a) * e1x + Sin(a) * e2x
			oy# = Cos(a) * e1y + Sin(a) * e2y
			oz# = Cos(a) * e1z + Sin(a) * e2z
			rad# = r0
			If ring = 1 Then rad = r1
			px# = x0 + dx * length * ring + ox * rad
			py# = y0 + dy * length * ring + oy * rad
			pz# = z0 + dz * length * ring + oz * rad
			v = AddVertex(s, px, py, pz, i * 1.0 * repeats / sides, ring * length / tile)
			BumpColor px, py, pz, -Sin(a) * e1x + Cos(a) * e2x, -Sin(a) * e1y + Cos(a) * e2y, -Sin(a) * e1z + Cos(a) * e2z, dx, dy, dz, ox, oy, oz, 0
			VertexColor s, v, CR, CG, CB
		Next
	Next
	For i = 0 To sides - 1
		bl = base + i
		br = base + i + 1
		tl = base + sides + 1 + i
		tr = tl + 1
		AddTriangle s, bl, tl, tr
		AddTriangle s, bl, tr, br
	Next
End Function

; Leaves on a branch: count single leaves along it (more towards the tip), each growing out of the branch on a short stem: it points away from the branch at 25 to 75 degrees, around the branch
; at random, tilts up and lies roughly flat, facing the light (turned a little around its own axis). Each is shaded to face away from the middle of the crown (cx, cy, cz) so that the
; outside of the crown is lit and the inside is dark.
Function LeafBranch(s, x0#, y0#, z0#, x1#, y1#, z1#, count, size#, spread#, cx#, cy#, cz#, r, g, b)
	dx# = x1 - x0
	dy# = y1 - y0
	dz# = z1 - z0
	dl# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz) + 0.0001
	dx = dx / dl : dy = dy / dl : dz = dz / dl
	For i = 1 To count
		t# = BenchRnd(0.15, 1.0)
		t = Sqr(t)
		px# = x0 + (x1 - x0) * t
		py# = y0 + (y1 - y0) * t
		pz# = z0 + (z1 - z0) * t
		; A direction at right angles to the branch, at random around it.
		rx# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
		ry# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
		rz# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
		dt# = rx * dx + ry * dy + rz * dz
		qx# = rx - dt * dx
		qy# = ry - dt * dy
		qz# = rz - dt * dz
		ql# = Sqr(qx * qx + qy * qy + qz * qz) + 0.001
		qx = qx / ql : qy = qy / ql : qz = qz / ql
		ang# = BenchRnd(25, 75)
		ux# = dx * Cos(ang) + qx * Sin(ang)
		; Leaves turn towards the light: the stem is flattened and tilts up, so that the blade faces up (to the moon) and not to the side.
		uy# = (dy * Cos(ang) + qy * Sin(ang)) * 0.4 + 0.4
		uz# = dz * Cos(ang) + qz * Sin(ang)
		ul# = Sqr(ux * ux + uy * uy + uz * uz)
		ux = ux / ul : uy = uy / ul : uz = uz / ul
		; The blade is wide sideways (at right angles to the leaf and to up), then turned around the leaf's own axis.
		wx# = uz : wy# = 0 : wz# = -ux
		wl# = Sqr(wx * wx + wz * wz)
		If wl < 0.05 Then
			wx = qx : wy = qy : wz = qz
		Else
			wx = wx / wl : wz = wz / wl
		EndIf
		roll# = BenchRnd(-30, 30)
		cx2# = uy * wz - uz * wy
		cy2# = uz * wx - ux * wz
		cz2# = ux * wy - uy * wx
		vx# = wx * Cos(roll) + cx2 * Sin(roll)
		vy# = wy * Cos(roll) + cy2 * Sin(roll)
		vz# = wz * Cos(roll) + cz2 * Sin(roll)
		nx# = px - cx : ny# = py - cy : nz# = pz - cz
		l# = Sqr(nx * nx + ny * ny + nz * nz) + 0.001
		shade# = BenchRnd(0.8, 1.15)
		sz# = size * LEAFSCALE * BenchRnd(0.8, 1.2)
		cell = Int(Floor(BenchRnd(0, 3.99)))
		out# = 0.5 + 0.5 * (ny / l)
		AddLeaf s, px, py, pz, ux, uy, uz, vx, vy, vz, sz, nx / l, ny / l * 0.5 + 0.5, nz / l, r * shade * (0.6 + 0.5 * out), g * shade * (0.6 + 0.5 * out), b * shade * (0.6 + 0.5 * out), cell
	Next
End Function

; Trunks are not straight tubes: the middle of the trunk wanders a little to the side as it goes up (TrunkOX, TrunkOZ), it is thicker and thinner by turns (TrunkR), and it flares out
; into roots at the foot. TrunkPh (a different one for every tree) and TrunkAmp (how crooked) say how.
Function TrunkOX#(y#)
	Return TrunkAmp * (Sin(y * 47 + TrunkPh) + 0.5 * Sin(y * 113 + TrunkPh * 2)) * (0.3 + 0.2 * y)
End Function

Function TrunkOZ#(y#)
	Return TrunkAmp * (Cos(y * 41 + TrunkPh * 3) + 0.5 * Sin(y * 97 + TrunkPh)) * (0.3 + 0.2 * y)
End Function

Function TrunkR#(y#, h#, rb#, rt#)
	r# = (rb + (rt - rb) * (y / h)) * (1 + 0.16 * Sin(y * 190 + TrunkPh * 5) + 0.08 * Sin(y * 430 + TrunkPh))
	flare# = 1 - y / 0.9
	If flare < 0 Then flare = 0
	Return r * (1 + 1.1 * flare * flare)
End Function

; The trunk, in 9 pieces from a little under the ground up to height h, rb thick at the bottom and rt at the top.
Function AddTrunk(s, h#, rb#, rt#)
	SwayOn = 0
	For i = 0 To 8
		y0# = h * i / 9
		y1# = h * (i + 1) / 9
		If i = 0 Then y0 = -0.25
		AddBranch s, TrunkOX(y0), y0, TrunkOZ(y0), TrunkOX(y1), y1, TrunkOZ(y1), TrunkR(y0, h, rb, rt), TrunkR(y1, h, rb, rt), 8
	Next
	SwayOn = 1
End Function

; A branch that branches: a tube from (x, y, z) in direction (dx, dy, dz) for length, rad thick, down to depth 0. The branch is not straight: it is three pieces, each bent a little from the one before, and it
; gets thinner along its length. A branch of length 2 has nchild side branches, a longer one more and a shorter one fewer, so that every branch has as many as it can carry; none grow from the lower
; third (the tree lost its low branches as it grew), and the nearer to the tip, the shorter they are (shrink times the length of the parent), so that the crown is a cone or a dome and not a mess. They leave
; at ang degrees in random directions around the branch, leaning up a little, and are 0.6 times as thick. Leaves sit only on the thin branches (depth 0: many, depth 1: a few), so that the thick parts
; of the tree are bare wood, and the leaves sit on twigs, the twigs on small branches and those on boughs, as on a real tree. (cx, cy, cz) is the middle of the crown, for the shading.
Function Grow(s, ls, x#, y#, z#, dx#, dy#, dz#, length#, rad#, depth, nchild, ang#, shrink#, leafn, size#, r, g, b, cx#, cy#, cz#)
	x0# = x : y0# = y : z0# = z
	sides = 3
	If rad > 0.03 Then sides = 4
	If rad > 0.05 Then sides = 6
	; Leaves on the pieces of thin branches only: a twig (depth 0) has the most.
	leaves = 0
	spreadl# = size * 0.3
	If depth = 0 Then
		leaves = leafn / 3
		spreadl = size * 0.4
	EndIf
	If depth = 1 Then leaves = leafn / 8
	; Piece 1: bent a little from the one before.
	dl# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
	dx = dx / dl : dy = dy / dl : dz = dz / dl
	d0x# = dx : d0y# = dy : d0z# = dz
	x1# = x0 + dx * length / 3
	y1# = y0 + dy * length / 3
	z1# = z0 + dz * length / 3
	AddBranch s, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, rad * 1.0000, rad * 0.8392, sides
	LeafBranch ls, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, leaves, size, spreadl, cx, cy, cz, r, g, b
	; Piece 2: bent a little from the one before.
	dx = dx + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dy = dy + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dz = dz + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dl# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
	dx = dx / dl : dy = dy / dl : dz = dz / dl
	d1x# = dx : d1y# = dy : d1z# = dz
	x2# = x1 + dx * length / 3
	y2# = y1 + dy * length / 3
	z2# = z1 + dz * length / 3
	AddBranch s, x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, rad * 0.8833, rad * 0.7283, sides
	LeafBranch ls, x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, leaves, size, spreadl, cx, cy, cz, r, g, b
	; Piece 3: bent a little from the one before.
	dx = dx + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dy = dy + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dz = dz + BenchRnd(-1, 1) * 0.3
	dl# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)
	dx = dx / dl : dy = dy / dl : dz = dz / dl
	d2x# = dx : d2y# = dy : d2z# = dz
	x3# = x2 + dx * length / 3
	y3# = y2 + dy * length / 3
	z3# = z2 + dz * length / 3
	AddBranch s, x2, y2, z2, x3, y3, z3, rad * 0.7667, rad * 0.6175, sides
	LeafBranch ls, x2, y2, z2, x3, y3, z3, leaves, size, spreadl, cx, cy, cz, r, g, b
	If depth > 0 Then
		kids = Int(nchild * length / 2.0 + 0.5)
		If kids < 2 Then kids = 2
		For i = 1 To kids
			t# = 0.33 + 0.67 * (i - 0.5) / kids
			; The piece the child grows from, and where on it.
			sdx# = d2x : sdy# = d2y : sdz# = d2z
			px0# = x2 : py0# = y2 : pz0# = z2 : px1# = x3 : py1# = y3 : pz1# = z3
			f# = t * 3 - 2
			If t < 0.6667 Then
				sdx = d1x : sdy = d1y : sdz = d1z
				px0 = x1 : py0 = y1 : pz0 = z1 : px1 = x2 : py1 = y2 : pz1 = z2
				f = t * 3 - 1
			EndIf
			If t < 0.3333 Then
				sdx = d0x : sdy = d0y : sdz = d0z
				px0 = x0 : py0 = y0 : pz0 = z0 : px1 = x1 : py1 = y1 : pz1 = z1
				f = t * 3
			EndIf
			rx# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
			ry# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
			rz# = BenchRnd(-1, 1)
			dt# = rx * sdx + ry * sdy + rz * sdz
			qx# = rx - dt * sdx
			qy# = ry - dt * sdy
			qz# = rz - dt * sdz
			pl# = Sqr(qx * qx + qy * qy + qz * qz) + 0.001
			a# = ang * BenchRnd(0.75, 1.2)
			ndx# = sdx * Cos(a) + qx / pl * Sin(a)
			ndy# = sdy * Cos(a) + qy / pl * Sin(a) + 0.1
			ndz# = sdz * Cos(a) + qz / pl * Sin(a)
			nl# = Sqr(ndx * ndx + ndy * ndy + ndz * ndz)
			sl# = length * shrink * (1.15 - 0.6 * t) * BenchRnd(0.8, 1.1)
			Grow s, ls, px0 + (px1 - px0) * f, py0 + (py1 - py0) * f, pz0 + (pz1 - pz0) * f, ndx / nl, ndy / nl, ndz / nl, sl, rad * 0.6, depth - 1, nchild, ang, shrink, leafn, size, r, g, b, cx, cy, cz
		Next
	EndIf
End Function

; A tree: kind 0 is a spruce (a trunk, bare below, with rings of four or five branches that sit closer together and get shorter towards the top, each with side twigs), 1 a broadleaf tree (a trunk that forks into five boughs, each
; branching twice more) and 2 a birch (a slim trunk with thin boughs that go up and branch once). variant shifts the colors. The mesh is the trunk and the branches, with a second mesh as its
; child that holds the leaf cards, which sit on the twigs (leaves is how many cards a twig has).
Function MakeTree(kind, variant, leaves)
	CurTpl = kind * 3 + variant + 1
	TplFirst(kind * 3 + variant) = SwayN
	m = CreateMesh()
	s = CreateSurface(m)
	lm = CreateMesh(m)
	ls = CreateSurface(lm)
	k# = 1 + (variant - 1) * 0.12
	TrunkPh = BenchRnd(0, 360)
	Select kind
		Case 0
			TrunkAmp = 0.06
			AddTrunk s, 7.4, 0.22, 0.03
			For w = 0 To 10
				; The lowest branches died off under the higher ones, so the trunk is bare there. The rings sit closer together towards
				; the top and the branches get shorter.
				u# = w / 10.0
				y# = 2.3 + 4.9 * (1 - (1 - u) * Sqr(1 - u))
				length# = 2.3 - 1.95 * u
				wn = 4
				If w > 5 Then wn = 5
				For i = 0 To wn - 1
					ang# = i * 360.0 / wn + w * 41 + variant * 11
					ox# = TrunkOX(y)
					oz# = TrunkOZ(y)
					Grow s, ls, ox, y, oz, Cos(ang) * 0.97, -0.2, Sin(ang) * 0.97, length, 0.05 * (length / 2.2 + 0.3), 2, 4, 62, 0.45, leaves, 0.85, 52 * k, 100 * k, 62 * k, 0, y + 1.5, 0
				Next
			Next
			LeafBranch ls, 0, 7.0, 0, 0, 8.0, 0, leaves * 2, 0.8, 0.2, 0, 6, 0, 60 * k, 110 * k, 68 * k
		Case 1
			TrunkAmp = 0.12
			AddTrunk s, 3.0, 0.32, 0.2
			For i = 0 To 4
				ang# = i * 72 + variant * 17
				yb# = 2.6 + (i Mod 2) * 0.4
				Grow s, ls, TrunkOX(yb), yb, TrunkOZ(yb), Cos(ang) * 0.7, 0.7, Sin(ang) * 0.7, 2.3, 0.13, 3, 3, 42, 0.62, leaves, 0.95, 66 * k, 120 * k, 52 * k, 0, 4.2, 0
			Next
			LeafBranch ls, 0, 4.6, 0, 0, 5.6, 0, leaves * 2, 1.0, 0.7, 0, 4.2, 0, 70 * k, 124 * k, 54 * k
		Default
			TrunkAmp = 0.16
			AddTrunk s, 5.2, 0.16, 0.05
			For i = 0 To 6
				ang# = i * 51 + variant * 23
				y# = 2.0 + i * 0.45
				Grow s, ls, TrunkOX(y), y, TrunkOZ(y), Cos(ang) * 0.6, 0.8, Sin(ang) * 0.6, 1.6, 0.05, 2, 3, 38, 0.6, leaves, 0.85, 120 * k, 160 * k, 60 * k, 0, 4.2, 0
			Next
			LeafBranch ls, 0, 5.0, 0, 0, 5.8, 0, leaves * 2, 0.9, 0.5, 0, 4.2, 0, 128 * k, 168 * k, 64 * k
	End Select
	EntityFX m, 1 + 2
	EntityTexture m, NormalBark, 0, 0
	If kind = 2 Then
		EntityTexture m, AlbedoBirch, 0, 1
	Else
		EntityTexture m, AlbedoBark, 0, 1
	EndIf
	EntityFX lm, 2 + 16
	EntityTexture lm, leaftexture
	TplCount(kind * 3 + variant) = SwayN - TplFirst(kind * 3 + variant)
	CurTpl = 0
	Return m
End Function

; A pebble: a flat dome of five corners that sits half in the ground.
Function AddPebble(s, x#, y#, z#, rad#, tone, rot#, tint)
	; Dark grey stones, now and then with a reddish (1) or bluish (2) tone.
	rt# = 1 : gt# = 1 : bt# = 1
	If tint = 1 Then rt = 1.35 : gt = 0.9 : bt = 0.85
	If tint = 2 Then rt = 0.85 : gt = 0.95 : bt = 1.35
	base = CountVertices(s)
	For i = 0 To 4
		a# = i * 72 + rot
		v = AddVertex(s, x + Cos(a) * rad, y - rad * 0.1, z + Sin(a) * rad)
		VertexColor s, v, tone * 0.8 * rt, tone * 0.78 * gt, tone * 0.76 * bt
	Next
	top = AddVertex(s, x, y + rad * 0.55, z)
	VertexColor s, top, tone * rt, tone * 0.98 * gt, tone * 0.95 * bt
	For i = 0 To 4
		AddTriangle s, base + i, top, base + ((i + 1) Mod 5)
	Next
End Function

; Boards, posts and rails of an old bridge from the near bank to the far bank over the river, wide 2.6 units, with bumps (and the torch light fixed in them): weathered grey wood
; with moss, a deck that has sagged, boards that are missing or broken and a fence that is not straight.
; The post positions of the bridge (the original needs arrays to be declared in the main program).
Dim brpx#(6)
Dim brptop#(6)
Dim brpz#(6)
Dim brplx#(6)
Dim brplz#(6)

Function MakeBridge()
	m = CreateMesh()
	s = CreateSurface(m)
	x0# = BridgeX - BRIDGEHALF
	x1# = BridgeX + BRIDGEHALF
	; Two beams under the boards, not quite the same length and not quite level.
	For side = -1 To 1 Step 2
		e0# = BenchRnd(-0.2, 0.1)
		e1# = BenchRnd(-0.1, 0.2)
		dy# = BenchRnd(-0.02, 0.02)
		AddBoxB s, x0 - 0.3 + e0, 0.85 + dy - 0.05, side * 0.9 - 0.1, x1 + 0.3 + e1, 1.06 + dy - 0.05, side * 0.9 + 0.1
	Next
	; The boards: different widths, gaps, lengths and heights, as if they were cut by hand and have settled.
	x# = x0
	While x < x1 - 0.3
		wdt# = BenchRnd(0.34, 0.47)
		gap# = BenchRnd(0.012, 0.055)
		top# = 1.2 + BenchRnd(-0.015, 0.015)
		z0# = -1.3 + BenchRnd(-0.07, 0.04)
		z1# = 1.3 + BenchRnd(-0.04, 0.07)
		; It has sagged in the middle, boards are missing, and one is a broken stump.
		t# = (x - BridgeX) / BRIDGEHALF
		sag# = -0.09 * (1 - t * t)
		gone# = BenchRnd(0, 1)
		If gone < 0.07 And x > x0 + 0.5 And x < x1 - 0.8 Then
			; missing
		ElseIf gone < 0.12 And x > x0 + 0.5 And x < x1 - 0.8 Then
			AddBoxB s, x, 1.06 + sag, z0, x + wdt, top + sag, z0 + BenchRnd(0.5, 0.9)
		Else
			AddBoxB s, x, 1.06 + sag, z0, x + wdt, top + sag, z1
		EndIf
		x = x + wdt + gap
	Wend
	; The fence on each side: seven posts that are not evenly spaced, not equally tall, thick or straight, with a rail along the top and one in the middle between
	; them that is cut into pieces, one of which is missing in places. The posts are round, and so are the rails.
	For side = -1 To 1 Step 2
		For i = 0 To 6
			jitter# = BenchRnd(-0.25, 0.25)
			If i = 0 Or i = 6 Then jitter = jitter * 0.3
			brpx(i) = x0 + 0.1 + i * (x1 - x0 - 0.2) / 6 + jitter
			brpz(i) = side * 1.2 + BenchRnd(-0.05, 0.05)
			brptop(i) = 1.9 + BenchRnd(-0.1, 0.14)
			brplx(i) = BenchRnd(-0.05, 0.05)
			brplz(i) = BenchRnd(-0.06, 0.06)
			r0# = BenchRnd(0.065, 0.1)
			AddBranch s, brpx(i), 1.0, brpz(i), brpx(i) + brplx(i), brptop(i), brpz(i) + brplz(i), r0, r0 * 0.85, 6
		Next
		For i = 0 To 5
			; The top rail: one piece from post to post, a little past them and not level.
			ra# = BenchRnd(0.02, 0.07)
			rb# = BenchRnd(0.02, 0.07)
			rr# = BenchRnd(0.035, 0.055)
			AddBranch s, brpx(i) + brplx(i) * 0.9 - ra, brptop(i) - 0.1 + BenchRnd(-0.03, 0.03), brpz(i) + brplz(i) * 0.9, brpx(i + 1) + brplx(i + 1) * 0.9 + rb, brptop(i + 1) - 0.1 + BenchRnd(-0.03, 0.03), brpz(i + 1) + brplz(i + 1) * 0.9, rr, rr * 0.9, 5
			; The middle rail, which is missing in one piece in six.
			gone# = BenchRnd(0, 1)
			If gone > 0.17 Then
				rr = BenchRnd(0.03, 0.045)
				AddBranch s, brpx(i) + brplx(i) * 0.5, 1.5 + BenchRnd(-0.05, 0.05), brpz(i) + brplz(i) * 0.5 + 0.02, brpx(i + 1) + brplx(i + 1) * 0.5, 1.5 + BenchRnd(-0.05, 0.05), brpz(i + 1) + brplz(i + 1) * 0.5 - 0.02, rr, rr * 0.9, 5
			EndIf
		Next
	Next
	; Piles that go down into the river.
	For side = -1 To 1 Step 2
		For i = 0 To 1
			x = BridgeX - 2.5 + i * 5 + BenchRnd(-0.3, 0.3)
			AddBoxB s, x - 0.14, BEDY, side * 0.9 - 0.14, x + 0.14, 1.06, side * 0.9 + 0.14
		Next
	Next
	EntityFX m, 1 + 2
	EntityTexture m, NormalPlanks, 0, 0
	EntityTexture m, AlbedoPlanks, 0, 1
	Return m
End Function

; A flame as eight pictures of it (frames of one texture), each a teardrop that sways and flickers a little differently: white-yellow where it is hottest at the bottom,
; orange in the middle and red and dark at the tip and the edge. It is added to what is behind it, so what is dark is not there.
Function MakeFlame()
	t = CreateTexture(64, 128, 3, 8)
	For f = 0 To 7
		SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t, f)
		LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t, f)
		For y = 0 To 127
			hh# = (127 - y) / 127.0
			sway# = 0.18 * Sin(hh * 400 + f * 45) * hh
			width# = (0.28 + 0.6 * Sin(Sqr(hh) * 180)) * ((1 - hh) ^ 0.5) + 0.001
			For x = 0 To 63
				u# = (x - 31.5) / 31.5
				turb# = 0.12 * Sin(hh * 900 + u * 250 + f * 80) * hh + 0.08 * Sin(hh * 1500 - f * 120 + u * 90)
				d# = 1 - Abs(u - sway - turb * 0.5) / width
				If d < 0 Then d = 0
				i# = d ^ 0.8
				temp# = i * (1.15 - hh * 0.9)
				If temp > 1 Then temp = 1
				cg# = temp * 1.3
				If cg > 1 Then cg = 1
				cb# = (temp - 0.65) * 3
				If cb < 0 Then cb = 0
				If cb > 1 Then cb = 1
				WritePixelFast x, y, (Int(i * 255) Shl 24) Or (Int(i * 255) Shl 16) Or (Int(i * cg * 255) Shl 8) Or Int(i * cb * 255), TextureBuffer(t, f)
			Next
		Next
		UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t, f)
	Next
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; A wave crest: a thin bright arc (a crescent, wider than high, curving downstream) that fades out at its ends and sides, to be added to the water.
Function MakeCrest()
	t = CreateTexture(128, 64, 3)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 63
		For x = 0 To 127
			u# = (x - 63.5) / 63.5
			v# = y / 63.0
			cy# = 0.35 + 0.3 * u * u
			d# = Abs(v - cy) / 0.09
			a# = 1 - d
			If a < 0 Then a = 0
			e# = 1 - Abs(u) ^ 1.6
			If e < 0 Then e = 0
			a = a * a * e
			c = Int(a * 255)
			WritePixelFast x, y, (c Shl 24) Or (c Shl 16) Or (c Shl 8) Or c, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; A soft round puff: opaque white in the middle, see-through at the edge.
Function MakePuff()
	t = CreateTexture(32, 32, 3 + 4096)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 31
		For x = 0 To 31
			dx# = (x - 15.5) / 15.5
			dy# = (y - 15.5) / 15.5
			r# = Sqr(dx * dx + dy * dy)
			a# = 1 - r
			If a < 0 Then a = 0
			a = a * a * (3 - 2 * a)
			WritePixelFast x, y, (Int(a * 255) Shl 24) Or $FFFFFF, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; The leaves: four single leaves of different shapes, one in each quarter of the texture (64 x 64 texels each): pointed, a little broader at the stem (the left), curved to one side
; and with a light midrib and side veins, darker towards the edge. Cut out by alpha (flags 2 and 4) with grey where nothing is, so no dark border shows.
Function MakeLeaves()
	t = CreateTexture(128, 128, 1 + 2 + 4 + 8)
	SetBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	LockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	For y = 0 To 127
		For x = 0 To 127
			WritePixelFast x, y, $00B0B0B0, TextureBuffer(t)
		Next
	Next
	For cell = 0 To 3
		ox = (cell And 1) * 64
		oy = (cell Shr 1) * 64
		wide# = 0.36 + 0.05 * cell
		bend# = (cell Mod 3 - 1) * 5.0
		For y = 0 To 63
			For x = 0 To 63
				u# = (x - 32) / 28.0
				v# = (y - 32) - bend * u * u
				If Abs(u) < 1 Then
					hw# = wide * 28 * (1 - u * u) ^ 0.7 * (1 - 0.3 * u)
					If Abs(v) < hw Then
						c = 205 - Int(70 * Abs(v) / hw)
						side# = Abs(v) - (u + 1) * 6
						If Abs(Sin(side * 55)) < 0.16 Then c = c + 25
						If Abs(v) < 1.3 Then c = 255
						WritePixelFast ox + x, oy + y, $FF000000 Or (c Shl 16) Or (c Shl 8) Or c, TextureBuffer(t)
					EndIf
				EndIf
			Next
		Next
	Next
	UnlockBuffer TextureBuffer(t)
	SetBuffer BackBuffer()
	BenchFilter t
	Return t
End Function

; One blade of grass, opaque, dark at the root and light at the tip. A tall blade has five vertices (two at the root, two halfway up and the tip) and three triangles and curves, a short one
; has three and one triangle. It leans away from straight up in direction leandir, with the tip further out than the middle. The blade is w wide at the root and h tall. Returns the
; number of the tip, which is the only vertex that moves in the wind.
Function AddBlade(s, x#, y#, z#, w#, h#, rot#, leanamount#, leandir#, tint#)
	dx# = Cos(rot) * w
	dz# = Sin(rot) * w
	lx# = Cos(leandir) * leanamount * h
	lz# = Sin(leandir) * leanamount * h
	base = CountVertices(s)
	v = AddVertex(s, x - dx, y, z - dz)
	VertexColor s, v, 26 * tint, 56 * tint, 20 * tint
	v = AddVertex(s, x + dx, y, z + dz)
	VertexColor s, v, 26 * tint, 56 * tint, 20 * tint
	If h < 0.35 Then
		v = AddVertex(s, x + lx, y + h, z + lz)
		VertexColor s, v, 110 * tint, 170 * tint, 66 * tint
		For k = 0 To 2
			VertexNormal s, base + k, 0, 1, 0
		Next
		AddTriangle s, base, base + 2, base + 1
		Return base + 2
	EndIf
	v = AddVertex(s, x - dx * 0.65 + lx * 0.3, y + h * 0.55, z - dz * 0.65 + lz * 0.3)
	VertexColor s, v, 60 * tint, 120 * tint, 40 * tint
	v = AddVertex(s, x + dx * 0.65 + lx * 0.3, y + h * 0.55, z + dz * 0.65 + lz * 0.3)
	VertexColor s, v, 60 * tint, 120 * tint, 40 * tint
	v = AddVertex(s, x + lx, y + h, z + lz)
	VertexColor s, v, 118 * tint, 176 * tint, 72 * tint
	For k = 0 To 4
		VertexNormal s, base + k, 0, 1, 0
	Next
	AddTriangle s, base, base + 2, base + 3
	AddTriangle s, base, base + 3, base + 1
	AddTriangle s, base + 2, base + 4, base + 3
	Return base + 4
End Function

; The area (8 x 8 areas of 20 x 20 units) a place belongs to.
Function AreaOf(x#, z#)
	ax = Int(Floor((x + WORLD) / 20))
	az = Int(Floor((z + WORLD) / 20))
	If ax < 0 Then ax = 0
	If ax > 7 Then ax = 7
	If az < 0 Then az = 0
	If az > 7 Then az = 7
	Return az * 8 + ax
End Function

; The waves of the river: every vertex of the ribbon goes up and down, in waves that run down the river (along z, 9 degrees per frame) with ripples across them, and
; the normals are made again, so that the water has a new shape every frame.
Function RunWater(g#)
	For i = 0 To 160
		z# = -WORLD + i
		For c = 0 To 5
			y# = WATERY + 0.05 * Sin(z * 22 - g * 9 + c * 55) + 0.03 * Sin(z * 57 - g * 14 - c * 80) + 0.02 * Sin(c * 130 + g * 6)
			VertexCoords watersurf, i * 6 + c, RiverX(z) - 5 + c * 2, y, z
		Next
	Next
	UpdateNormals water
End Function

; Smallest power of two that holds n (the original needs texture sizes to be powers of two).
Function Pow2(n)
	p = 1
	While p < n
		p = p * 2
	Wend
	Return p
End Function

; A flat square from -1 to 1 that shows the top left u x v part of its texture. A camera 1 unit in front of it, with the default field of view, sees exactly this square
; (scale it by the viewport's height divided by its width in y).
Function MakeQuadUV(u#, v#)
	m = CreateMesh()
	s = CreateSurface(m)
	AddVertex s, -1, 1, 0, 0, 0
	AddVertex s, 1, 1, 0, u, 0
	AddVertex s, 1, -1, 0, u, v
	AddVertex s, -1, -1, 0, 0, v
	AddTriangle s, 0, 1, 2
	AddTriangle s, 0, 2, 3
	EntityFX m, 1 + 8 + 16
	Return m
End Function

; One step of the bloom: the camera draws the world in front of it into the top left of the back buffer, and what it drew is copied into a texture.
Function BloomRender(cam, vw, vh, tex)
	CameraViewport cam, 0, 0, vw, vh
	CameraProjMode cam, 1
	RenderWorld
	If tex <> 0 Then CopyRect 0, 0, vw, vh, 0, 0, BackBuffer(), TextureBuffer(tex)
	CameraProjMode cam, 0
End Function

Graphics3D Int(Env$("BENCH_W", 640)), Int(Env$("BENCH_H", 360)), 32, 2
SetBuffer BackBuffer()

treecount = Int(Env$("BENCH_TREES", 1800))
grasscount = Int(Env$("BENCH_GRASS", 600000))
leafcards = Int(Env$("BENCH_LEAVES", 18))
pebblecount = Int(Env$("BENCH_PEBBLES", 14000))
insects = Int(Env$("BENCH_INSECTS", 40))
insectlights = Int(Env$("BENCH_INSECT_LIGHTS", 6))
frames = Int(Env$("BENCH_FRAMES", 600))
warmup = Int(Env$("BENCH_WARMUP", 5))
startframe = Int(Env$("BENCH_START", 0))
seed = Int(Env$("BENCH_SEED", 1))
viewriver = Int(Env$("BENCH_VIEWRIVER", 0))
If frames < 1 Then frames = 1
If insectlights > insects Then insectlights = insects

BenchSeedRnd seed
BridgeX = RiverX(0)

; The sky at dusk, and fog that hides the end of the world.
camera = CreateCamera()
CameraClsColor camera, 10, 15, 30
CameraRange camera, 0.3, 140
CameraFogMode camera, 1
CameraFogColor camera, 10, 15, 30
CameraFogRange camera, 25, 120
AmbientLight 38, 46, 68

; The sky is a sphere that follows the camera and is drawn first, without light and fog, and the full moon is a sprite in front of it. The moon stands
; low in the east (the camera walks along the east-west path), and its light comes from there.
moondir# = 0
sky = CreateSphere(24)
ScaleEntity sky, 100, 100, 100
EntityFX sky, 1 + 8 + 16
EntityTexture sky, MakeStars()
EntityOrder sky, 100
moonsprite = CreateSprite()
EntityTexture moonsprite, MakeMoon()
EntityFX moonsprite, 1 + 8
EntityOrder moonsprite, 99
ScaleSprite moonsprite, 5.7, 5.7

; The first light is the moon, then the torch, then the insects: the original Blitz3D uses the first 8 in this order.
moon = CreateLight()
LightColor moon, 120, 138, 190
MoonX = Cos(22) * Cos(18)
MoonY = Sin(22)
MoonZ = Cos(22) * Sin(18)
