; The picture of the water is drawn on the GPU every frame: a second camera, far away from the world, looks at a flat scene of drifting wave crests (thin arcs that run with the
; river), glints that flicker and big, faint swells, all added together on a deep blue-green, and what it sees is copied into a texture (a render target,
; flag 4096). The camera is 5 units from the scene with a field of 90 degrees, so it sees 10 x 10 units, which is the width of the river and 10 units of its length.
; Everything wraps from the bottom to the top of the picture, so that the picture repeats along the river.
crest = MakeCrest()
watertex = CreateTexture(256, 256, 1 + 256 + 4096)
EntityTexture water, watertex
watercam = CreateCamera()
PositionEntity watercam, 5000, 0, -5
